id: pm-gh1778
title: "GH-1778: pm context extension_health reports ok for packages with a known update and prints same-named project and global copies as identical rows"
description: "GH-1778 (filed 2026-11-24). pm context ends with an extension_health block whose rows are {name,status}: status comes only from static discovery, so a package with a known newer registry version reads ok, and a package installed in both project and global scope prints two identical rows with nothing saying which copy the runtime loads (project shadows global by name in buildEffectiveExtensions). pm context is the orientation call agents run first, so ok: 3 reads as nothing to do; the report's hub ran extensions seven weeks behind for that reason. Constraint: pm context must stay offline and fast, and update lookups are network calls that pm package manage and pm package doctor make but never persist (last_update_remote_version is documented as never persisted). Companion finding in the same command: an invalid --section value is refused with a recovery bundle that lists only 8 of the 10 valid sections and says allowed_values_omitted: 2 (complete domain via SDK error.context.recovery.allowed_values), which a CLI agent cannot read; the human Next steps line lists all 10. Small closed domains should print whole. Reproduced on 2026.11.25. Duplicate check: searched extension_health update available shadowed scope, recovery allowed values omitted; no open owner."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[6]: agent-ux,context,extensions,"gh:1778",packages,recovery
created_at: "2026-11-25T05:51:21.704Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-25T07:16:08.518Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-25T07:16:07.022Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-25T07:16:07.022Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "extension_health rows carry name, scope, version and status, plus the last observed newer registry version as update when one is known, without any network call from pm context; The summary carries updates_available and a next hint naming the update command only when that count is above zero; A copy shadowed by a same-named copy in another scope is marked shadowed_by instead of repeating an identical row; A refused enumerated value whose whole domain is small prints every allowed value in the recovery bundle, with no omitted counter"
parent: pm-ugqx
risk: medium
confidence: medium
reporter: unbraind
severity: medium
resolution: "pm package manage records each answered freshness check in the untracked runtime/extension-update-observations.json of its scope (failed lookups keep the earlier observation; a failed write only warns). pm context reads it offline: rows {name,scope,version,status,update,shadowed_by}, summary updates_available, and next with one pm package upgrade command per scope only when that count is above zero; an observation applies only to the installed version it was taken against. The markdown rendering names the update count and the commands. Human recovery prints a legal domain of 12 or fewer values whole at the unbudgeted limit, so a refused pm context --section lists all 10 sections; budgeted renderings keep their limits."
expected_result: "pm context tells an agent which installed packages have known updates and which copy is active, without a network call, and a refused section lists every valid section"
actual_result: "The report's setup reproduced in a sandbox now reads global pm-github shadowed_by project, project pm-github update 2026.11.23, updates_available 1, next pm package upgrade pm-github --project; pm context --section bogus lists all 10 sections; orientation cost rose by 23 tokens per session, inside the declared 3,000-token context budget"
